>> title: Salsa Roja
>> category: Sauces & Gravies
>> tags: tomato, chiles, mexican, vegetarian, stovetop
>> counters: Taquería
>> aka: roja, table salsa, salsa de mesa
>> servings: 6
>> time: 30 min

>> step: char 10 min
Char @Roma tomatoes{1%lb}(450 g), @white onion{1/2%medium}(thick slices), @garlic{3%cloves}(unpeeled; peel after charring), and @serrano chiles{2} on a dry #comal{} for ~{10%min}, turning until blistered all over.

>> step: blend coarse
Blend @&(~1)charred vegetables{} with @kosher salt{1%tsp} to a coarse purée.

>> step: fry 5 min
Fry @&(~1)salsa{} in @vegetable oil{1%Tbs} over high heat for ~{5%min}, until it darkens and pulls together.

>> step: finish off heat
Finish @&(~1)salsa{} off the heat with @cilantro{2%Tbs}(chopped) and @fresh lime juice{1%tsp}.
